{"id":1104,"date":"2026-05-08T13:38:21","date_gmt":"2026-05-08T11:38:21","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/?p=1104"},"modified":"2026-05-08T13:50:56","modified_gmt":"2026-05-08T11:50:56","slug":"accepted-papers-at-smps2026-conference","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/2026\/05\/08\/accepted-papers-at-smps2026-conference\/","title":{"rendered":"Accepted papers at SMPS&#8217;2026 Conference"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">The <a href=\"https:\/\/conference.unisalento.it\/event\/14\/\">12th International Conference on Soft Methods in Probability and Statistics (SMPS&#8217;2026 Conference)<\/a> will be held in Lecce (Italy) in 15-18 September, 2026.<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">We have submitted four papers, all of which have been accepted for presentation:<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\"><em><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\"><em>Testing convex-ordering dominance via OWA-based skewness coefficients<\/em><\/mark><\/em>, by Marina Iturrate-Bobes, Ignacio Montes and Ra\u00fal P\u00e9rez-Fern\u00e1ndez.<\/mark><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\"><em><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\"><em>Skewness coefficients for rounded data<\/em><\/mark><\/em>, by Marina Iturrate-Bobes, Ignacio Montes and Ra\u00fal P\u00e9rez-Fern\u00e1ndez.<\/mark><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\"><em><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\"><em>The Imprecise Kolmogorov Model for robustifying p-boxes<\/em><\/mark><\/em>, by David Nieto-Barba, Ignacio Montes and Enrique Miranda.<\/mark><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\"><em><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\"><em>Measuring incoherence for lower probabilities<\/em><\/mark><\/em>, by Juan Jes\u00fas Salamanca, Enrique Miranda and Ignacio Montes.<\/mark><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">Moreover, we are organising the special session: <em>Theoretical and applied aspects of imprecise probabilities<\/em> (by Enrique Miranda and Ra\u00fal P\u00e9rez-Fern\u00e1ndez).<\/mark><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-black-color\">Looking forward to seeing you in Lecce!<\/mark><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The 12th International Conference on Soft Methods in Probability and Statistics (SMPS&#8217;2026 Conference) will be held in Lecce (Italy) in 15-18 September, 2026. We have submitted four papers, all of which have been accepted for presentation: Moreover, we are organising the special session: Theoretical and applied aspects of imprecise probabilities (by Enrique Miranda and Ra\u00fal&#8230;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1001,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-1104","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-sin-categoria"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/1104","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types